From 136707c5bf9637d046c40c66eb32d4445b013d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alvaro Moran <alvaro.moran@huggingface.co>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(model): add a Transformers modeling backend

Serve a Hugging Face *ForCausalLM with the modeling code of transformers,
as vLLM's Transformers modeling backend does on GPU (--model-impl
transformers). TransformersForCausalLM implements the Neuron runner
contract (from_configs, get_kv_spec, bind_kv_cache, load_weights, forward)
around AutoModelForCausalLM, and is registered under the name vLLM
resolves to for that option.

Attention goes through a function registered in the transformers
AttentionInterface ("neuron_paged"): it writes K/V to the paged cache at
the step's slots, then runs causal attention over the step's tokens on
prefill, or over each sequence's cache gathered from its block table on
decode and segmented prefill. It handles sliding windows, soft-capping
and attention sinks with plain PyTorch ops. The runner's attention
metadata reaches it through the transformers kwargs, and logits are only
computed at the sampling positions (logits_to_keep). Sampling uses the
on-device Sampler, which Model Runner V2 requires.

Tensor parallelism 1 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
